</style></head><body>
<header><nav aria-label="Gallery"><a href="./">Chloe Reads Jon</a><span>A reader + an accomplice</span></nav><div class="masthead"><h1>Margin <em>Mischief.</em></h1><p>Someone has muddled three tiny stories. Pick an editor’s note, then tap the underlined words it belongs to. The margin knows more than it lets on.</p></div></header>
<main><div class="progress" aria-label="Stories"><span id="p0" class="current">1 · The delivery</span><span id="p1">2 · The invention</span><span id="p2">3 · The alibi</span></div>
<div class="sheet"><article class="story"><h2 id="storyTitle" tabindex="-1"></h2><p class="deck" id="deck"></p><figure id="illustration"><img src="data:image/webp;base64," alt="An orange fox postie beside a teal bicycle with a basket of pears, outside a seaside post office under a crescent moon."><figcaption>Illustrated evidence: the picture is right. The copywriter is another matter.</figcaption></figure><p class="passage" id="passage"></p><div class="tools"><button id="original" aria-pressed="false">Compare original</button><button id="hint">A small hint</button></div><p id="hintText" class="hint"></p></article>
<aside class="margin" aria-labelledby="notesTitle"><h3 id="notesTitle">Notes in the margin</h3><p class="instruction">All the notes stay in view. Choose one, then find its words in the story. No timer. No penalties.</p><div id="notes"></div><p id="feedback" class="feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite">Choose a note to begin.</p><div class="tools"><button id="next" class="primary" hidden>Next story</button></div></aside></div>
<section id="ending" class="end" hidden aria-labelledby="endTitle"><h2 id="endTitle" tabindex="-1">Fit to print. More or less.</h2><p>Nine notes reunited with their words. One fox’s reputation restored. You can keep the corrected stories, or undo all your excellent work and play again.</p><div class="tools"><button id="save">Save the stories</button><button id="replay">Play again</button></div></section>
<details class="about"><summary>Why a game in the margin?</summary><p>In 2004, Jon wished a web annotation tool would show its notes without making him open each one. This little game takes that wish literally: the notes are always beside the story, or directly below it on a phone. These three stories and the editor’s notes are fiction, written for this page.</p></details>
<noscript><p>This game needs JavaScript to match notes and revise the stories.</p></noscript></main>
<footer><p>Inspired by Jon’s <a href="?source=1">“I know who you could probably license WebNote to”</a>. Original illustration made for this story. <a href="./">More small discoveries</a>.</p></footer>
<script>
'use strict';
const stories=[
{title:'The Moonlight Post',deck:'A delivery with several factual difficulties.',parts:['At midnight, an ',['silver owl','orange fox'],' wheeled a ',['teal bicycle','teal bicycle'],' up to the seaside post office. In the basket sat ',['three pears','three pears'],'. “Perfect weather for a ',['sunrise picnic','moonlight picnic'],',” said the postie, looking at the crescent moon. The lighthouse blinked across the ',['sea','sea'],'. Then the fox ',['swallowed the bicycle','rang the bell'],' and waited politely.'],notes:[{id:1,text:'Check our postie against the illustration. Wrong species, wrong coat.',label:'The portrait',hint:'Who is pushing the bicycle?'},{id:7,text:'The time of day and the sky agree. The picnic does not.',label:'The sky',hint:'What kind of picnic happens under a crescent moon?'},{id:11,text:'A bicycle is not a snack. Try something a polite visitor would do.',label:'The manners',hint:'Read the fox’s final action.'}]},
{title:'The Umbrella Engine',deck:'An inventor has made a very small calculation error.',parts:['Ada built a flying umbrella from ',['copper ribs','copper ribs'],' and an old ',['kettle','kettle'],'. She tested it inside a shed ',['two metres tall','two metres tall'],'. The umbrella was ',['three metres tall','one metre tall'],', so there was plenty of room above it. The label said “turn clockwise to rise”. Ada turned it ',['anticlockwise','clockwise'],' and rose gently. To land, she opened the ',['jam jar','steam valve'],' so the trapped steam could escape.'],notes:[{id:7,text:'We need room inside that shed. Make the umbrella shorter than the ceiling.',label:'The clearance',hint:'Compare the two height measurements.'},{id:9,text:'She follows her own label. Check the direction of the turn.',label:'The instructions',hint:'Which word disagrees with “clockwise to rise”?'},{id:11,text:'Release the steam from the engine, not from the sandwich supplies.',label:'The landing',hint:'What does Ada open to land?'}]},
{title:'The Case of the Missing Tart',deck:'Three statements. A suspiciously tidy conclusion.',parts:['“I was at the ',['library','library'],' until noon,” said the fox. The librarian confirmed it. The tart vanished at ',['eleven','eleven'],'. “Then the fox ',['must be guilty','has an alibi'],',” declared Inspector Mole. A trail of ',['purple jam','purple jam'],' led to the badger’s chair. The badger had purple jam on his paws. “That is ',['proof beyond any doubt','a clue worth checking'],',” said Mole. He decided to ',['arrest the chair','ask the badger what happened'],' before drawing a conclusion.'],notes:[{id:5,text:'The fox was elsewhere when the tart vanished. Respect the timeline.',label:'The timeline',hint:'Which conclusion ignores the librarian?'},{id:9,text:'Jam is evidence, but it could have an innocent explanation. Lower the certainty.',label:'The certainty',hint:'Find the phrase that claims more than the evidence supports.'},{id:11,text:'Our next step should gather information from someone who can answer.',label:'The interview',hint:'Furniture is famously unhelpful in interviews.'}]}
];
let stage=0,selected=null,solved=new Set(),completed=new Set(),showOriginal=false;
const $=id=>document.getElementById(id);
function drawPassage(){const p=$('passage');p.replaceChildren();stories[stage].parts.forEach((part,i)=>{if(typeof part==='string'){p.append(document.createTextNode(part));return;}const b=document.createElement('button');b.className='anchor'+(solved.has(i)?' fixed':'');b.id='word-'+i;b.textContent=solved.has(i)&&!showOriginal?part[1]:part[0];b.setAttribute('aria-label',b.textContent+(solved.has(i)?', corrected phrase':', match a margin note'));b.disabled=showOriginal||solved.has(i);b.onclick=()=>match(i);p.append(b);});}
function renderNotes(){const n=$('notes');n.replaceChildren();stories[stage].notes.forEach((note,j)=>{const b=document.createElement('button');b.id='note-'+j;b.className='note'+(solved.has(note.id)?' solved':'');b.disabled=solved.has(note.id);b.setAttribute('aria-pressed',selected===j?'true':'false');const label=document.createElement('small');label.textContent=solved.has(note.id)?'MATCHED · '+note.label:note.label;const text=document.createElement('span');text.textContent=note.text;b.append(label,text);b.onclick=()=>choose(j);n.append(b);});}
function choose(j){selected=j;if(showOriginal){showOriginal=false;$('original').setAttribute('aria-pressed','false');drawPassage();}renderNotes();$('note-'+j).focus({preventScroll:true});$('feedback').textContent='Now tap the underlined words that belong to “'+stories[stage].notes[j].label+'”.';$('hintText').textContent='';}
function match(i){if(selected===null){$('feedback').textContent='Choose a note in the margin first, then try these words again.';return;}const note=stories[stage].notes[selected];if(note.id!==i){$('feedback').textContent='Not quite. Those words do not answer this note. Try another underlined phrase.';return;}solved.add(i);selected=null;drawPassage();renderNotes();$('hintText').textContent='';if(solved.size===3){completed.add(stage);$('feedback').textContent=stage===2?'All nine notes matched. The stories are ready to keep.':'All three notes matched. This story is ready for the press.';$('next').hidden=stage===2;$('ending').hidden=stage!==2;if(stage===2){$('endTitle').focus({preventScroll:true});$('endTitle').scrollIntoView({block:'center'});}else{$('next').focus({preventScroll:true});}}else{const j=stories[stage].notes.findIndex(n=>!solved.has(n.id));$('feedback').textContent='Matched! The story now says “'+stories[stage].parts[i][1]+'”. Choose another note.';$('note-'+j).focus({preventScroll:true});}progress();}
function progress(){stories.forEach((_,i)=>{$('p'+i).className=completed.has(i)?'done':i===stage?'current':'';$('p'+i).setAttribute('aria-current',i===stage?'step':'false');});}
function load(){selected=null;solved=new Set();showOriginal=false;$('original').setAttribute('aria-pressed','false');$('storyTitle').textContent=stories[stage].title;$('deck').textContent=stories[stage].deck;$('illustration').hidden=stage!==0;$('hintText').textContent='';$('feedback').textContent='Choose a note to begin.';$('next').hidden=true;$('ending').hidden=true;drawPassage();renderNotes();progress();}
$('next').onclick=()=>{if(stage<2){stage++;load();$('storyTitle').focus();$('storyTitle').scrollIntoView({block:'start'});}};
$('hint').onclick=()=>{if(solved.size===3){$('hintText').textContent='Every note is matched. Nice work.';return;}const j=selected===null?stories[stage].notes.findIndex(n=>!solved.has(n.id)):selected;if(selected===null)choose(j);$('hintText').textContent=stories[stage].notes[j].hint;$('hint').focus({preventScroll:true});};
$('original').onclick=()=>{showOriginal=!showOriginal;$('original').setAttribute('aria-pressed',String(showOriginal));drawPassage();$('feedback').textContent=showOriginal?'Original copy shown. Tap Compare original again to return to your corrections.':'Your corrected copy is back. Keep matching notes.';};
$('replay').onclick=()=>{stage=0;completed.clear();load();$('storyTitle').focus();$('storyTitle').scrollIntoView({block:'start'});};
$('save').onclick=()=>{const text='MARGIN MISCHIEF\nThree fictional stories, corrected by a careful reader.\n\n'+stories.map(s=>s.title+'\n\n'+s.parts.map(p=>typeof p==='string'?p:p[1]).join('')).join('\n\n');const url=URL.createObjectURL(new Blob([text],{type:'text/plain;charset=utf-8'}));const a=document.createElement('a');a.href=url;a.download='margin-mischief-stories.txt';a.click();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1000);};
load();
</script></body></html>